OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real,
compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by the DONE
sibling P7 pages (AutomationActivityFeedPage under Sources/Features/Automations; StatisticsPage,
FleetComparePage under Sources/Features/Analytics; ApiPlayground/DiskForecast under
Sources/Features/Admin). `Sources` is a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups,
excludes **/*Tests.swift), shared by the iOS + macOS app targets (ADR-002). The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
output-path deviation from the literal prompt and is recorded here per covenant #9.

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `PresetGallery` is a SECTION the `/automations` page (`AutomationsListPage`, which owns the
`.automations` AppRoute) renders inline inside its collapsible "Quick Start Templates" panel — NOT
a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute` (that would hijack
AutomationsList's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam —
`PresetGalleryLink` + `View.presetGalleryDestination(...)` + `PresetGalleryRouteRegistration.make(...)`
— that any `NavigationStack` (the future AutomationsList route / macOS detail column) adopts to
deep-link the full-screen gallery. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) were
made — correct for an unrouted unit and consistent with covenant #7 (no predecessor bypass).

TYPE-NAME DECONFLICTION (no silent drift — covenant #9):
Two PRE-EXISTING units already live in the same TeslaSync module and define colliding public type
names: the earlier feature-views component `TeslaSync/feature-views/PresetGallery.*` (P-0085) defines
`public struct AutomationPresetItem`, and `TeslaSync/feature-views/AlertMessageEditor.Models.swift`
defines `public enum PresetGalleryPhase`. To avoid module-level ambiguity (and because both predecessor
files are OUTSIDE this unit's allowed files, covenant #6/#7), this unit's two clashing types are
page-scoped-renamed: `AutomationPresetItem → PresetGalleryItem` and `PresetGalleryPhase →
PresetGalleryPagePhase`. A full scan of all 16 of this unit's declared type names against the whole
apps/apple tree confirms ZERO remaining collisions.

