PRE-EXISTING, OUT-OF-SCOPE BUILD BREAKAGE (forbidden to commit-fix — covenant #6/#7)
================================================================================
The full `xcodebuild` app target does not link at this HEAD due to PRE-EXISTING source errors in
SIBLING surfaces OUTSIDE this artifact's allowed files. The blocking error (the same diagnostic class
repeated across four files):

  apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AISignalExplorerNlFilter.swift:142:22:
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions.swift:141:22:
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AISuggestNewGeofences.swift:
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations.swift:
    error: escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'

Root cause (NOT mine): each of those four sibling files declares a local helper
`private func glass(@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View)` whose `content` parameter is
NON-escaping, then passes it into `TSGlassPanel { content() }` whose initializer takes an
`@escaping () -> Content`. That is a genuine pre-existing compile error in those other parity units'
files. `git status --porcelain` shows all four are tracked and UNMODIFIED by me. My PresetCard /
PresetCardSkeleton use `TSGlassPanel` correctly (trailing-closure literals), so MY files do NOT
exhibit the anti-pattern (`grep '() -> some View)' Sources/Features/Automations/PresetGallery*.swift`
= none).

This is the same DISPOSITION CLASS recorded for every other in-flight Apple parity unit in
`apps/macos-pending-verifications.md` (e.g. ToolCard, AlertMessageEditor, FSMTimelineChart,
EnergyChargingPanel, MediaNavigationPanel, PowertrainPanel, …): the surface is verified green in
isolation, the full-app `xcodebuild build test` is blocked by pre-existing, unrelated parallel-merge
breakage in OTHER agents' files, and is deferred to the `p4-apple/P99-0001-apple-acceptance-gate`. It
is forbidden to commit-fix (covenant #6/#7) and is NOT in scope for this unit.

